---
import Button from '../../components/Button.astro';
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { sitePath } from '../../lib/siteUrl';
import StatusPill from '../../components/StatusPill.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Shader Effects"
  description="Use curated, editable effects in Varve with optional GPU compute, deterministic controls, CPU fallback, and honest export behavior."
>
  <div class="container-custom">
    <main class="feature-page">
      <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href={sitePath('/features')}>Features</a> / Shader Effects
      </nav>

      <header class="page-hero">
        <div class="eyebrow"><StatusPill status="available" /> <span>Curated effects with optional GPU compute</span></div>
        <h1>Give pixels a point of view. Keep the design editable.</h1>
        <p>
          Varve’s shader effects turn print screens, optical bloom, analog signal, refracted light,
          and other treatments into ordinary editable effect entries. Tune the result on the
          selected object, then keep the recipe, order, mask, blend mode, and source content intact.
        </p>
      </header>

      <section class="feature-section feature-section--highlight" aria-labelledby="workflow-title">
        <p class="eyebrow">A creative workflow, not a shader playground</p>
        <h2 id="workflow-title">Choose a treatment. Adjust it. Ship the same idea.</h2>
        <div class="workflow-grid">
          <article><span>01</span><h3>Select</h3><p>Pick a shape, image, text object, or group and add a curated effect from the existing Effect Studio and Object Filters surfaces.</p></article>
          <article><span>02</span><h3>Author</h3><p>Use meaningful controls for scale, angle, origin, colors, intensity, seed, and quality. Before/After comparison keeps experiments reversible.</p></article>
          <article><span>03</span><h3>Export</h3><p>Export uses the committed document recipe and requested bounds. The authoritative software path remains available when an optional accelerator cannot complete.</p></article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="feature-section" aria-labelledby="families-title">
        <h2 id="families-title">Effects for texture, optics, and signal.</h2>
        <div class="card-grid">
          <article><h3>Print and palette</h3><p>Palette Snap and the halftone family help build screen-printed, newsprint, riso, and reduced-color looks while retaining the source.</p></article>
          <article><h3>Light and lens</h3><p>Bloom, Light Shafts, Lens Flare, Light Leak, and Caustics provide controllable atmosphere with explicit intensity and spatial parameters.</p></article>
          <article><h3>Analog signal</h3><p>CRT, VHS, and RGB Split keep seeds and frame parameters stable, so a repaint, pan, or reopened document does not invent a new look.</p></article>
          <article><h3>Stack and mask</h3><p>Effects participate in the normal order, opacity, blend, scope, mask, history, and duplication workflows. Vector and text editability remains separate from the rendered treatment.</p></article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="feature-section feature-section--highlight" aria-labelledby="trust-title">
        <h2 id="trust-title">Acceleration is optional. The result is not.</h2>
        <dl class="trust-list">
          <div><dt>WebGPU or native compute</dt><dd>Available to explicit asynchronous effect consumers only after the device, shader contract, and request are usable. The current interactive preview and export replay stay on the authoritative software path; diagnostics distinguish actual execution from API availability.</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Software fallback</dt><dd>CPU kernels remain the compatibility path for Linux WebKitGTK, older browsers, software adapters, and device loss. The document is never held hostage by a GPU.</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Honest export</dt><dd>Effects are evaluated at export quality and correct bounds. SVG/PDF preserve unaffected vector and text content, rasterizing only the dependency region that cannot be represented structurally.</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Offline-first</dt><dd>Ordinary effects require no cloud compiler, model download, hidden network request, or arbitrary code execution.</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </section>

      <section class="feature-section">
        <h2>Why this feels different from “turn on GPU acceleration.”</h2>
        <p>
          Creative tools have taught users to distrust GPU switches that cause flicker, blank
          canvases, corrupted color, or a frozen export. Varve keeps acceleration per operation,
          observes compilation and device errors, bounds its resources, and returns to the tested
          software implementation when a device cannot complete the request. A fallback is visible
          in diagnostics; it is not a silent change to the authored parameters.
        </p>
        <p><a href={sitePath('/docs/tools/shader-effects')}>Read the Shader Effects guide</a> or <a href={sitePath('/features/effect-studio')}>explore Effect Studio</a>.</p>
      </section>

      <div class="feature-cta">
        <h2>Make the effect yours, then keep editing.</h2>
        <Button href={sitePath('/download')}>Download Varve</Button>
      </div>
    </main>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .feature-page { max-width: 860px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 3rem 0 5rem; }
  .breadcrumb { color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: .875rem; margin-bottom: 2.5rem; }
  .breadcrumb a, .feature-section a { color: var(--text-link); }
  .page-hero { max-width: 720px; margin-bottom: 4rem; }
  .eyebrow { align-items: center; color: var(--accent-primary); display: flex; font-size: var(--type-interface-micro-size); font-weight: 700; gap: .65rem; letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .page-hero h1 { color: var(--text-primary); font: 700 clamp(2.3rem, 6vw, 4rem)/1.05 var(--font-editorial); letter-spacing: -.025em; margin: 1rem 0; }
  .page-hero p, .feature-section p, .trust-list dd { color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.75; }
  .feature-section { margin: 0 0 4rem; }
  .feature-section h2 { color: var(--text-primary); font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 3vw, 2.3rem); margin: .5rem 0 1rem; }
  .feature-section h3 { color: var(--text-primary); margin: .65rem 0 .45rem; }
  .feature-section--highlight { background: var(--surface-card); border: 1px solid var(--border-default); border-radius: var(--website-radius-card); padding: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 3rem); }
  .workflow-grid, .card-grid { display: grid; gap: 1rem; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); margin-top: 1.75rem; }
  .workflow-grid article, .card-grid article { border: 1px solid var(--border-default); border-radius: var(--website-radius-surface); padding: 1rem; }
  .workflow-grid span { color: var(--accent-primary); font-size: var(--type-interface-micro-size); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .workflow-grid p, .card-grid p { font-size: .95rem; margin: 0; }
  .trust-list { display: grid; gap: .85rem; margin: 1.5rem 0 0; }
  .trust-list div { border-left: 2px solid var(--border-accent); padding-left: 1rem; }
  .trust-list dt { color: var(--text-primary); font-weight: 700; }
  .trust-list dd { margin: .2rem 0 0; }
  .feature-cta { border-top: 1px solid var(--border-default); padding-top: 2.5rem; text-align: center; }
  .feature-cta h2 { color: var(--text-primary); font-size: 1.35rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  @media (max-width: 680px) { .workflow-grid, .card-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .feature-page { padding-top: 2rem; } }
</style>
